    "summary": "High‑energy Hill Auditorium show with stellar Dark Star and Lovelight suite",
    "blurb": "Features a soaring Dark Star, an explosive Turn On Your Lovelight sequence and tight interplay throughout. Jerry’s guitar shines while Keith’s piano dominates the mix, and Phil provides a steady bass foundation.",
    "review": "December 15, 1971 at Hill Auditorium captures one of the Dead's most electric late‑year outings. The band launches into a blistering first set that includes a ripping Bertha, crisp runs on Mr. Charlie and a punchy Run Rudolph Run before winding down with a heartfelt Brokedown Palace. The second set erupts with a menacing Dark Star that segues into a tight Deal, followed by an exuberant Turn On Your Lovelight → I'm A King Bee → Mannish Boy sandwich that showcases Keith Godchaux’s piano front‑and‑center and Bill Kreutzmann’s confident drumming. The night closes on high spirits with Sugar Magnolia, a final turn of the Lovelight medley, and a jubilant encore of One More Saturday Night and Uncle John’s Band. Across all available soundboard tapes the performance is consistently high‑octane, with Jerry’s sky‑high leads, Phil’s solid bass undercurrent, Bob’s controlled vocals, and Keith’s fiery keyboards driving the jams.",
